    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_b35f3167d0d74120a5cd377d",
      "name": "semantic_search",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 20, \"items_by_type\": {\"metric\": [{\"id\": \"dw_1023\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year where the Mathematics department has at least one unique subject with subject enrollment number greater than 10, what are the academic year, academic year description, department name, number of unique subjects, minimum total units offered, variance of total units, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units for subjects offered in the fall term that are not variable units and are offered by the Mathematics department? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1301\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, where the maximum number of total units for any Mathematics (Course 18) subject offered in that year is greater than 9 and there are more than 5 Mathematics subjects offered in the fall term, what are the academic year, the maximum total units, the corresponding term description, the subject title, the academic year description, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in library subjects offered during terms in that year, and the average number of equivalent subjects for those library subjects? List the results in order of academic year. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1393\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year and department in Mathematics, what is the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered in that year and department (considering only subjects offered in the current term, with more than 0 total units, and with subject enrollment number greater than the average for that department and year), and for those departments, what are the department code, corresponding administrative department name, the graduate level of courses, and the total number of distinct courses per department, for all degree-granting departments except the Management department? Present the results as academic year, department name, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), department code, administrative department name, graduate level, and number of distinct courses, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4229\", \"desc\": \"For IAP subjects in the \\\"Mathematics\\\" category, show the activity title, enrollment type, maximum enrollment, category name, activity description, and the row number within each enrollment type group ordered by activity title, along with the academic year, department name, average enrollment, enrollment variance, department phone number, and school name for each academic year and department where the IAP subject's term matches a department's fall term subject offering with more than 0 enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2272\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department, what is the department name, the average of the total units, the range of the total units, the variance of the total units for courses with total units greater than 0, and for each course level, what is the number of unique students and the minimum CIP program code among their courses, considering only degree-granting departments? Additionally, for each course level, what is the average number of lecture units and the maximum number of lab units for Mathematics courses? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1335\", \"desc\": \"List, for each department, either (a) the department's full name, the range and variance of the total units for degree-granting Mathematics department courses offered in the 2008 academic year along with the long course description for each course (with the reason 'Math 2008 Stats'), or (b) the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units) where the average total units is greater than the overall average across all departments (with the reason 'High Avg Units'). Show the columns in the following order: department name, total units range, total units variance, average total units, standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, long course description, and reason for inclusion. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_41\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, provide the academic year description and calculate the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered in terms that are not the current term, have a term status indicator of 'P', are offered by the Mathematics department, and are full term subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1288\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the maximum enrollment for IAP activities offered in that year by the Mathematics department, considering only activities that require advance sign-up and are not cancelled, and also provide the academic year description? For each department, include a grand total for all activities in the format of (department name, null, total variance and stddev). Additionally, for each such department, provide the department code, the department name, and the total number of enrolled students in both the library and tip subject offerings, but only for those departments where the total number of enrolled students is more than one standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) above the mean total enrolled students across all departments, and restrict your answer to departments whose name is 'Mathematics' (Course 18). Also, for each such department, list the names of the responsible faculty members from both the library and tip subject offerings. The columns to display, in order, are: department name, academic year description, total variance, total standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), department code, department name, total enrolled, library faculty, and tip faculty. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2377\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the department's name, the range and variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the academic year 2022 and that are also listed in the CIS course catalog, and for all course subjects in the catalog where the department code is 18 (Mathematics), the department name is 'Mathematics', and the subject is offered this year, show the subject code, subject number, responsible faculty's full name, Moira list member, the average office phone number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the responsible faculty's last name and ordered by the subject code, and the email address of the responsible faculty. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2335\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level, where the total number of enrolled students in offered subjects is greater than 10, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the number of unique courses, the minimum total units among those subjects that are degree-granting courses, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for Mathematics courses (considering only departments that offer more than five courses), and the number of unique subject codes for Mathematics in the SIS_SUBJECT_CODE table. List the department name, course level, number of unique courses, minimum total units, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, and the number of unique subject codes, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2158\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the 2022 academic year by a degree-granting department, specifically in the Department of Mathematics (Course 18) and excluding subjects offered by the Department of Physics, provide the subject ID, subject title, department name, the number of enrolled students, the total number of lecture units, and, for each subject, indicate whether it is also offered as a joint subject with another department. Additionally, show the range and variance of the total units for letter graded subjects offered this year in the Mathematics department. List the results in order of subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1758\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with total units equal to 12 in the Mathematics department, show the department code, department name, subject code, subject number, subject title, total units, the row number within each department ordered by subject code, the deviation of each subject's total units from the average total units of all Mathematics subjects offered in 2024, the number of enrolled students, responsible faculty name, school name, and the dense rank over the department name ordered by department name for those subjects that also have course materials and were offered in the term '2019FA'. Sort the table by department name and subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1766\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level where the course is degree granting, the total units are greater than 6, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the department name, course level, number of unique courses, minimum total units offered, school name, number of distinct course options available, and the highest average number of enrolled students in any term for courses offered by that department, considering only courses with more than 0 enrolled students and departments whose name is not null. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2180\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2014FA' by the Chemistry department, show the subject title from the library, the number of enrolled students in the library subject, the responsible faculty name from the TIP subject, the offer department name from the TIP subject, the minimum number of enrolled students in the library subject within a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the TIP subject's responsible faculty MIT ID, and for each academic year, also show the academic year and academic year description and the coefficient of variation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects in the Mathematics department (Course 18) that have more than 0 total units and are offered in terms with a term status indicator of 'P'. Additionally, for each Chemistry subject, include the number of required TIP materials (where TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'RQ') for that subject in that term. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_5150\", \"desc\": \"How many subjects in the course catalog are offered in the spring term, have a total of at least 6 units, are taught by faculty who are responsible for at least one subject with more than 0 enrolled students according to the subject offered summary, and are in the Mathematics department (Course 18)? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4658\", \"desc\": \"Show the Mathematics department courses with at least 5 enrolled students, including the course number, subject title, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, the row number within each academic year group ordered by course number, the term start date, calendar date, day of week, the average calendar year within each calendar year group ordered by term start date, and for each course, also display the responsible faculty name and the offer school name, but only for academic terms where the term status is 'Previous'. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2365\", \"desc\": \"For the top 3 most frequently offered courses in the Mathematics department, for each course and each term it was offered, display the course number, course description, subject title, number of times offered, department name, number of unique course descriptions for that course and department, the minimum CIP program code for that course and department, the term code, the term description, the school name, and the department phone number. Do not repeat the course number if it is the same as the previous row. Sort the table by course number and term code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1049\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department, what is the department name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for its subjects in regular terms that are not the current term, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2022 academic year (considering only departments that have more than five subjects offered in 2022, are degree-granting, and are not the Chemistry department)? Show the department name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) for regular non-current terms, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) for 2022. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1471\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units in the Mathematics department (Course 18), show the subject code, subject title, department name, school name, and the rank within each school name group ordered by subject code, but only include those subjects whose total units exceed the average total units for their respective school. Additionally, for the Mathematics department, also show the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects that are offered this year, are letter graded, and are in the Mathematics department), as well as the number of subjects that are Communication Intensive (i.e., have a non-null COMM_REQ_ATTRIBUTE), with these statistics included for each subject in the result. Present the columns in the following order: subject code, subject title, department name, school name, rank within school, average total units, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), and number of Communication Intensive subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4640\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the term '2017JA', what is the subject title, the number of enrolled students, the responsible faculty name, the offering department name, the department full name, the school name, the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the department code, the coefficient of variation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in the subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with at least one enrolled student), and the department's school code? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}}"
    },
    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_d2fbb5cf3818473eb9bd0325",
      "name": "semantic_get",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"entities\": [{\"id\": \"concept_subject_offering_facts\", \"name\": \"Subject Offering Fact Tables\", \"desc\": \"Fact tables recording subjects offered per term from different business processes: the course catalog (planned catalog attributes), the registrar's section/subject offering records (actual sections and enrollment), subject-level summaries (final enrollment statistics), the textbook information program (subjects tracked for course materials), and library reserve processing (subjects with library reserve activity). They share subject identity (SUBJECT_ID, TERM_CODE) and department attribution but differ in granularity, enrollment semantics, and available measures.\", \"tables\": [\"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Granularity\", \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"Subject offering per term/academic year (catalog record, includes section flags)\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"Subject section per term (finest grain, SECTION_ID)\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\": \"Subject per term (rollup of sections)\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\": \"Subject or cluster per term\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"Subject per term within textbook program scope\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"Subject per term within library reserve scope\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Enrollment measures\", \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"None (catalog attributes only)\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER, SECTION_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER, CLUSTER_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\": \"NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER, CLUSTER_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\": \"SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER plus first-week/fifth-week and credit/listener enrollment splits\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Unit measures\", \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"LECTURE_UNITS, LAB_UNITS, PREPARATION_UNITS, DESIGN_UNITS, TOTAL_UNITS, IS_VARIABLE_UNITS\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"None\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\": \"TOTAL_UNITS, LECTURE_UNITS, LAB_UNITS, PREPARATION_UNITS\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\": \"TOTAL_UNITS, LECTURE_UNITS, LAB_UNITS, PREP_UNITS, DESIGN_UNITS\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"None\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"None\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Distinctive attributes\", \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"HGN_DESC level, GRADE_TYPE/GRADE_RULE, HASS/GIR attributes, IS_OFFERED_* flags, MEET_PLACE (room key), ACADEMIC_YEAR, EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"IS_REPEATABLE_SUBJECT, CLUSTER_TYPE, section flags, FORM_TYPE, EVALUATE_THIS_SUBJECT\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\": \"OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME, COURSE_NUMBER, cluster info at subject level\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\": \"SCHOOL_CODE/SCHOOL_NAME, SUBJECT_GROUP_ID, SUBJECT_OR_CLUSTER, detailed weekly enrollment\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL flag; parent of TIP_DETAIL materials\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"COURSE_NUMBER/COURSE_NUMBER_DESC; parent of LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Department column naming\", \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"DEPARTMENT_CODE / DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"OFFER_DEPT_CODE / OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\": \"OFFER_DEPT_CODE / OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\": \"DEPARTMENT_CODE / DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"OFFER_DEPT_CODE / OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"OFFER_DEPT_CODE / OFFER_DEPT_NAME\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Questions about credit units, grading type/rules, HGN level (undergraduate/graduate), HASS/GIR attributes, or term offering flags (fall/spring/IAP/summer)\": \"Use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED; it is the only offering table carrying full catalog attributes.\", \"Questions about actual section-level offerings, repeatability, cluster type, or section flags\": \"Use SUBJECT_OFFERED (section grain); roll up via SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY when subject-level totals are needed.\", \"Questions about final enrollment statistics, weekly enrollment snapshots, credit vs listener counts, subject groups, or school-level unit statistics\": \"Use SUBJECT_SUMMARY.\", \"Questions about textbooks/course materials per subject (required/optional status, ISBN, record counts)\": \"Start from TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED (subject scope, IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL) joined to TIP_DETAIL (material rows).\", \"Questions about library reserve materials, reserve counts per subject, or library course numbers\": \"Start from LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED joined to LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.\", \"Questions about subject-level units with offering department/school (e.g. Engineering school enrollment totals by department)\": \"Use SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, which carries both TOTAL_UNITS and OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME.\"}}, {\"id\": \"concept_academic_term_dimension\", \"name\": \"Academic Term Dimension\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing academic terms and their calendar/status attributes. They jointly answer questions about when terms run, which academic/financial-aid/degree year a term belongs to, and whether a term is current, previous, future, or regular. Coverage differs: the full historical term list, the status-tracked term subset, and the three-row relative term parameter reference.\", \"tables\": [\"ACADEMIC_TERMS\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\", \"ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Row coverage\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\": \"Terms with full status tracking (subset of all terms)\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\": \"All terms known to the warehouse (superset of ACADEMIC_TERMS)\", \"ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER\": \"Exactly 3 rows: current, previous, and upcoming term\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Unique columns\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\": \"IS_REGULAR_TERM, TERM_STATUS ('Previous'/'Current'/'Future'/'Unspecified'), ADD_DATE, DROP_DATE\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\": \"No IS_REGULAR_TERM/TERM_STATUS/ADD_DATE/DROP_DATE; shares TERM_STATUS_INDICATOR, FINANCIAL_AID_YEAR, DEGREE_YEAR\", \"ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER\": \"TERM_PARAMETER name (SIS_CURRENT_TERM/SIS_PREVIOUS_TERM/SIS_UPCOMING_TERM), TERM_INDICATOR ('C'/'P'/'F'), TERM_LAST_DAY_BEFORE_NEXT_TERM\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Typical role in queries\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\": \"Filtering by regular-term flag or term status; term start/end dates and registration milestones\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\": \"Source of academic year, academic year description, financial aid year, degree year for windowed/running-sum statistics\", \"ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER\": \"Resolving relative term references ('current term', 'previous term', term indicator 'C'/'P') to concrete term codes\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Join keys\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\": \"TERM_CODE, ACADEMIC_TERMS_KEY\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\": \"TERM_CODE, ACADEMIC_TERMS_KEY\", \"ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER\": \"TERM_CODE\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Questions needing IS_REGULAR_TERM or TERM_STATUS ('Previous'/'Current'/'Future') filtering\": \"Use ACADEMIC_TERMS; these columns exist only there.\", \"Questions needing academic year, financial aid year, or degree year attributes over the widest term coverage, or joining fact tables whose terms may not be status-tracked\": \"Use ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL, optionally joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS on TERM_CODE when regular-term/status flags are also needed.\", \"Questions referring to 'the current term', 'the previous term', 'the upcoming term', or term indicator 'C'/'P'/'F'\": \"Use ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER to resolve the relative reference to a TERM_CODE, then join ACADEMIC_TERMS for full attributes.\", \"Questions needing registration milestones (add date, drop date, first day of classes, last day of final exam)\": \"Use ACADEMIC_TERMS (ADD_DATE/DROP_DATE only exist there; other milestone dates exist in both ACADEMIC_TERMS and ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL).\"}}, {\"columns\": [\"SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Measure meaning\", \"detail\": \"NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS is the headcount of students enrolled (present in SUBJECT_OFFERED at section grain, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY at subject grain, and in TIP/LIBRARY program snapshots); SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER is the official subject enrollment number recorded by the registrar (SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY)\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Grain\", \"detail\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS is per section; SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS is per subject per term; SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER is the final subject-level enrollment with weekly/credit/listener breakdowns available in sibling columns\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Program scope\", \"detail\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED and LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED enrollment values are snapshots within the textbook-program and library-reserve scopes respectively and may not cover all subjects\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Questions about official subject enrollment (e.g. 'subject enrollment number greater than 10')\": \"Use SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER.\", \"Questions about number of enrolled students per subject offering or per department totals\": \"Use NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS from SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (subject grain) or SUBJECT_OFFERED (section grain, needs aggregation).\", \"Questions about enrollment of subjects within the textbook program or library reserve scope\": \"Use TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS or LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS respectively.\", \"Questions needing enrollment timing (first week, fifth week) or credit vs listener splits\": \"Use SUBJECT_SUMMARY's SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_FIRST_WEEK / FIFTH_WEEK and *_CREDIT / *_LISTEN columns.\"}, \"desc\": \"Enrollment measure columns across subject offering, summary, textbook-program, and library tables. Two families exist: NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (student headcount snapshots) and SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (official registrar enrollment), at section, subject, or program scope.\", \"id\": \"column_concept_enrollment_measures\", \"name\": \"Enrollment Measures\"}, {\"columns\": [\"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\", \"CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS\", \"DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Source process\", \"detail\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS is the catalog-declared unit value per offering; SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS and SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS are registrar subject-level values; CIS/DRUPAL catalog feeds carry their own copies\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Companion unit columns\", \"detail\": \"All these tables also expose LECTURE_UNITS, LAB_UNITS, and preparation units (PREPARATION_UNITS except SUBJECT_SUMMARY which uses PREP_UNITS); DESIGN_UNITS exists in COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, CIS and DRUPAL catalogs but not in SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Variability flag\", \"detail\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.IS_VARIABLE_UNITS marks subjects whose units vary; analyses of fixed-unit statistics typically filter IS_VARIABLE_UNITS='N'\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Unit statistics (avg/stddev/variance/geometric mean) over catalog offerings, optionally split by lecture/lab/design or filtered by variable-units flag\": \"Use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS with its companion unit columns.\", \"Unit statistics tied to actual enrollment records or subject groups per term\": \"Use SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS.\", \"Unit statistics at subject-offering rollup level with offering department/school\": \"Use SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS.\", \"Fixed-unit analyses excluding variable-unit subjects\": \"Filter COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.IS_VARIABLE_UNITS = 'N'.\"}, \"desc\": \"Total credit unit columns replicated across catalog and registrar subject tables. They represent the same business quantity (total credit units of a subject) but come from different processes and pair with different companion unit columns.\", \"id\": \"column_concept_total_units\", \"name\": \"Total Credit Units\"}], \"not_found\": []}"
    },
